{"affected":[{"collectionURL":"https://cpan.org/modules","defaultStatus":"unaffected","modules":["JQ::Lite"],"original_ranges":[{"lessThan":"2.51","status":"affected","version":"0","versionType":"custom"}],"packageName":"JQ-Lite","packageURL":"pkg:cpan/JQ-Lite","programFiles":["lib/JQ/Lite/Util/Transform.pm"],"programRoutines":[{"name":"JQ::Lite::Util::_build_regex"}],"repo":"https://github.com/kawamurashingo/JQ-Lite"}],"aliases":["CVE-2026-78497"],"assertions":[{"affected_indices":[0],"descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"JQ::Lite versions before 2.51 for Perl execute Perl code embedded in a query's regular expression by compiling it with string eval.\n\nThe pattern given to test(), match(), or the match and =~ conditions of select() is placed in a `qr'...'` literal and compiled as source text, so a `(?{ ... })` code block in it runs without `use re 'eval'`. Single quotes in the pattern are escaped, but a code block runs in place and needs none.\n\nAn attacker who supplies a query, or text that an application inserts into the pattern of one, can execute arbitrary Perl code in the calling process."}],"problemTypes":[{"descriptions":[{"cweId":"CWE-95","description":"CWE-95 Improper Neutralization of Directives in Dynamically Evaluated Code ('Eval Injection')","lang":"en","type":"CWE"}]}],"provider":{"dateUpdated":"2026-10-18T11:32:05.853Z","orgId":"9b29abf9-4ab0-4765-b253-1875cd9b441e","shortName":"CPANSec"},"role":"cna","title":"JQ::Lite versions before 2.51 for Perl execute Perl code embedded in a query's regular expression by compiling it with string eval"}],"assessment":{"authentication":null,"classifier_version":"1.0","confidence":"unknown","configuration":null,"entry_protocol":null,"product_class":null,"reasons":[],"relevance":"unknown"},"content_hash":"f0b5b9489c07c6b43e57ac8992a863369672dadd0f2a79fc71874c196ed89c89","data_version":"5.2","first_seen_at":"2026-10-18T15:52:41Z","kind":"advisory","last_material_event_at":"2026-10-18T15:52:41Z","native_id":"CVE-20